spec.problem:
Clicking "Neuer Chat" / "New chat" does nothing once the current chat has messages. It only works when no chat is active or the active chat is empty. The cause is an inverted condition in `newChat` at `src/App.tsx:322-325`:

```ts
if (!active || active.messages.length === 0)
  dispatch({ type: "new", ... });
```

It creates a chat only when there is no active chat or the active chat is empty, which is the opposite of what was meant. The intent is clearly "do not stack up empty chats". So the button should do nothing only when the active chat is already empty, and create a new chat in every other case. Both buttons call this one handler: the sidebar button (`src/components/chat-sidebar.tsx:61`, wired at `src/App.tsx:342`) and the collapsed-sidebar chrome button (`src/components/sidebar-chrome.tsx:29`, wired at `src/App.tsx:345`). The reducer case `"new"` in `src/lib/chat/store.ts:73-85` works correctly (it prepends a chat and makes it active) and needs no change.

