spec.problem:
When a generation fails, the chat never leaves the "generating" state. In `src/App.tsx`, `send()` calls `setGenerating(true)` at line 237. It calls `setGenerating(false)` only on the success path, at line 261 inside the `try`. The `catch` block (276-284) records the error on the message with the `fail` action, which is why "Something went wrong: ..." appears (`src/components/message.tsx:64-69`). It never resets `generating`, and neither does the `finally` (285-288). So `generating` stays `true` for good. As a result:
- the composer keeps showing the Stop button and blocks sending (`src/components/chat-composer.tsx:40,80,92`);
- `send()` returns early (`App.tsx:221`);
- chats are no longer saved to localStorage (`App.tsx:172`).

Only a reload clears it, which matches the report. Stop cannot help because `inFlight` is already `null` after the `finally`.

